            <value>Quebec</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:SOREM:1.0:Broadcast_Text</valueName>
            <value>At 5:33 p.m. Eastern Daylight Time Tuesday, Environment Canada has issued a tornado warning for Southwestern Quebec. Extra care and attention should be exercised in and around the following localities: the Laurentians. Environment Canada meteorologists are tracking a severe thunderstorm that is possibly producing a tornado. Damaging winds, large hail and locally intense rainfall are also possible. Take cover immediately if threatening weather approaches. Please consult local media for more information.</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>layer:EC-MSC-SMC:1.1:Designation_Code</valueName>
